From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "David J. Vandenburgh" <david@vandenburgh.co>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 11:00:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] usb_gadget: take the bulk packet size from the link speed

check_and_send_USB_ZLP() ends a transfer with a zero length packet
when its size is a multiple of the bulk packet size, and that size was
fixed by usb_max_packet_size in the config. The right value depends on
the speed the host connected at: 64 bytes at full speed, 512 at high
speed, 1024 at SuperSpeed. With one fixed value, enabling SuperSpeed
would end some transfers early at one speed or add a stray packet at
another.

Once FunctionFS enables the function, ask it for the IN endpoint's
descriptor for the current speed and use its wMaxPacketSize. The
config value stays as the fallback when the ioctl fails.
---
diff --git a/src/usb_gadget.c b/src/usb_gadget.c
index 74d9d2a..f44df9b 100644
--- a/src/usb_gadget.c
+++ b/src/usb_gadget.c
@@ -814,6 +814,19 @@ int handle_ffs_ep0(usb_gadget * ctx)
 
 				if (!status)
 				{
+					/* The link speed is only known now: take the bulk packet size from the
+					 * endpoint descriptor FunctionFS picked for it (64, 512 or 1024), so the
+					 * zero length packet check matches the speed the host connected at. */
+					struct usb_endpoint_descriptor ep_desc;
+
+					memset(&ep_desc, 0, sizeof(ep_desc));
+					if (ioctl(ctx->ep_handles[EP_DESCRIPTOR_IN], FUNCTIONFS_ENDPOINT_DESC, &ep_desc) >= 0 &&
+					    le16toh(ep_desc.wMaxPacketSize))
+					{
+						mtp_context->max_packet_size = le16toh(ep_desc.wMaxPacketSize) & 0x7FF;
+						PRINT_MSG("USB bulk max packet size for this link : %d bytes", mtp_context->max_packet_size);
+					}
+
 					ctx->stop = 0;
 					if( ctx->thread_not_started )
 						ctx->thread_not_started = pthread_create(&ctx->thread, NULL, io_thread, ctx);
